  user_input {
    user_response: "Create a front-end workspace application called \"IGCSE OS Map Maker\" designed for geography teachers to prepare map resources. The UI must mimic a presentation editor like Google Slides, structured in a default landscape layout.\n\n### UI Layout & Core Dimensions\n1. Canvas Workspace (Central Area):\n   - A fixed canvas representing an A3 page in landscape view. Hardcode the proportions to exactly match an A3 sheet (29.7cm x 42cm ratio).\n   - The workspace background should be a subtle gray, making the white A3 page boundary stark and clear.\n\n2. Left Sidebar (Collapsible Panel):\n   - A thumbnail panel displaying a preview list of created pages (slides). Include a \"Create New Page\" button.\n   - An \"Upload Maps/Legends\" zone accepting PDF or PNG/JPG inputs.\n\n### Rigid Sizing & Scaling Constraints (CRITICAL)\n- The application must strictly preserve the native resolution and dimensions of any uploaded map image. \n- Disallow any form of free resizing, aspect-ratio stretching, or corner-dragging handles on the images. Sizing must remain absolute to preserve the map\'s original scale.\n- When an image is uploaded or moved into the workspace, it acts as a layer that can be repositioned (dragged) anywhere over or off the edges of the fixed A3 canvas.\n\n### Image Manipulation Features\nFor any selected map layer on the workspace page, provide an overlay or toolbar with the following controls:\n1. Free Rotation: A rotation slider or tool to easily re-align maps that are skewed or printed at an angle, allowing them to square up perfectly with the A3 page borders.\n2. Hard Crop & Split: \n   - A box-cropping tool that slices a portion of the map (e.g., isolating a 1:50,000 map fragment or cutting off the map legend).\n   - A \"Send Crop to New Page\" button, which instantly duplicates the cropped snippet onto a brand new, clean A3 slide in the left sidebar\342\200\224allowing teachers to cleanly separate the map from its key/legend.\n\nUse a clean, modern design with Tailwind CSS. Implement the workspace using an HTML5 Canvas or absolute CSS positioning layers so dragging, cropping, and rotating work smoothly in real time. "
    items {
      text: "Create a front-end workspace application called \"IGCSE OS Map Maker\" designed for geography teachers to prepare map resources. The UI must mimic a presentation editor like Google Slides, structured in a default landscape layout.\n\n### UI Layout & Core Dimensions\n1. Canvas Workspace (Central Area):\n   - A fixed canvas representing an A3 page in landscape view. Hardcode the proportions to exactly match an A3 sheet (29.7cm x 42cm ratio).\n   - The workspace background should be a subtle gray, making the white A3 page boundary stark and clear.\n\n2. Left Sidebar (Collapsible Panel):\n   - A thumbnail panel displaying a preview list of created pages (slides). Include a \"Create New Page\" button.\n   - An \"Upload Maps/Legends\" zone accepting PDF or PNG/JPG inputs.\n\n### Rigid Sizing & Scaling Constraints (CRITICAL)\n- The application must strictly preserve the native resolution and dimensions of any uploaded map image. \n- Disallow any form of free resizing, aspect-ratio stretching, or corner-dragging handles on the images. Sizing must remain absolute to preserve the map\'s original scale.\n- When an image is uploaded or moved into the workspace, it acts as a layer that can be repositioned (dragged) anywhere over or off the edges of the fixed A3 canvas.\n\n### Image Manipulation Features\nFor any selected map layer on the workspace page, provide an overlay or toolbar with the following controls:\n1. Free Rotation: A rotation slider or tool to easily re-align maps that are skewed or printed at an angle, allowing them to square up perfectly with the A3 page borders.\n2. Hard Crop & Split: \n   - A box-cropping tool that slices a portion of the map (e.g., isolating a 1:50,000 map fragment or cutting off the map legend).\n   - A \"Send Crop to New Page\" button, which instantly duplicates the cropped snippet onto a brand new, clean A3 slide in the left sidebar\342\200\224allowing teachers to cleanly separate the map from its key/legend.\n\nUse a clean, modern design with Tailwind CSS. Implement the workspace using an HTML5 Canvas or absolute CSS positioning layers so dragging, cropping, and rotating work smoothly in real time. "
    }
  }
}
