  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Celebrating Functional Completion**\n\nI\'ve reached a significant milestone! The application has compiled flawlessly, and I\'ve successfully implemented all core functionalities as planned. Specifically, I\'ve enabled the teacher to upload and view images as map layers on a fixed A3 canvas. I\'ve also incorporated the ability to visually reposition these layers within the workspace.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built the \"IGCSE OS Map Maker\" workspace designed specifically for precision presentation and resource extraction.\n\nHere is a summary of the accomplishments:\n- **Presentation Architecture**: Implemented a responsive two-pane dashboard. The central pane acts as a rigid workspace that fits perfectly onto a simulated horizontal A3 paper canvas (1587x1122 pixels). It features continuous relative scaling, allowing map components to seamlessly flow on or off the board boundaries.\n- **Absolute Scale Protection Rules**: Built a native local image buffer system that respects and fixes the input map image resolutions permanently across uploads. There are zero scaling handles inside the interface\342\200\224meaning a map will remain 100% precise to its pixel dimensions. \n- **Workspace Navigation & Uploading**: Built a collapsible left-hand slide dashboard where you can upload PNG/JPEG scans securely without losing data formatting, switch between active map layouts, and manage multiple sub-pages smoothly.\n- **Floating Manipulation Toolbar**: Engineered a context-sensitive editing toolkit that automatically affixes itself once an image element is selected:\n  - **High-Precision Free Rotation Engine**: Features a slider and manual number field for executing pure matrix rotations (0\342\200\223360\302\260), making it effortless to square-up historical skewed contour maps.\n  - **Native Isolation Extraction**: A transparent boundary box mapping layer acts as the crop selector. Once \"Extract to New Page\" is pressed, the spatial dimensions, workspace offsets, and element matrix rotations are recalculated on an isolated 2D mapping canvas, cleanly snapshotting the isolated snippet right onto a newly appended slide."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 692790145
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
