  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have updated the application to fully support local PDF uploads!\n\n**Why it wasn\'t working initially:**\nBrowsers cannot natively render PDF documents inside `<canvas>` or `<img>` elements the same way they handle PNGs or JPGs. Additionally, the file input was missing `application/pdf` in its accepted file types list. \n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Added `pdfjs-dist`**: I installed the official Mozilla PDF.js library to parse pdf files natively in the browser. \n- **Built an Image Converter**: When you upload a PDF, the application now intercepts it, uses the PDF.js web-worker to extract the first page at a high-resolution print scale (roughly 300 DPI), and seamlessly drops it directly into your A3 canvas workspace as a standard image layer.\n- **Fixed the File Input**: The upload button now explicitly allows `.pdf` selections and features an animated loading indicator while the PDF is parsing."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
