  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Multi-Selection Methods**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to best implement multi-selection. The initial thought is to make the default left-click act as a selection tool, like drag-to-select or even simple clicking. The ultimate goal is to enable item grouping, which drives this investigation.\n\n\n**Implementing Toggle Selection**\n\nI\'ve successfully added `metaKey` and `ctrlKey` support to `ElementNode.tsx`. Now, clicking while holding Command (Mac) or Control (Windows) toggles the selection of individual items. Next, I\'m shifting focus to marquee selection using `Workspace.tsx`, where I\'ll implement dragging a bounding box to select multiple elements at once.\n\n\n**Adding Marquee Selection**\n\nOkay, the `onPointerDown` on the container is still clearing selections, which is the desired behavior. Now, I\'m working to implement marquee selection. I\'m adding a `selectionBox` state to `Workspace.tsx`. The goal is to draw a selection box when the user drags on the canvas background. This requires calculating coordinates relative to the canvas.\n\n\n**Calculating Canvas Coordinates**\n\nI\'ve been working on calculating canvas coordinates for marquee selection. I\'m using `getBoundingClientRect()` to get the canvas position. Then, I\'m normalizing the mouse coordinates by the zoom level and pixels per centimeter, to establish accurate selection box start and end points relative to the canvas. I\'ve successfully implemented `onPointerMove` and `onPointerUp` to update the selection box state, drawing a selection box as the user drags and releases.\n\n\n**Refining Selection Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the selection logic, specifically within the `Workspace.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on accurately identifying elements that fall within the marquee selection box. To do this, I\'m calculating the minimum and maximum X and Y coordinates. I am then checking each element for an AABB (Axis-Aligned Bounding Box) intersection with the selection box. Finally, selected elements\' IDs are dispatched to the store.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 154840246
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
